From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] shader_environment: read NVN's draw parameters from the draw

Ported from Frizti/Fritchii 24838bf43 (zortos293/Lichii #806, merged in Fritchii v5), described there
as "read NVN's draw parameters from the draw (AMD tall grass and reeds); NVIDIA unchanged" - their
note records Lost Woods at 59.1 against 58.9 fps with the same grass, so nothing moved on NVIDIA.

The draw's own parameters build the shader environment, instead of whatever was last recorded, so a
shader translated for one draw no longer reads another draw's parameters. On AMD that showed as wrong
tall grass and reeds.

What this can break: any environment field that used to come from the stale record now comes from the
draw. If a caller passes an incomplete draw, those fields are what the draw says rather than what the
last draw left behind - which is the point, but it is a behaviour change for every shader built
afterwards.

Measured or a guess: upstream measured no change on NVIDIA and attributes the AMD symptom to this. Our
own logs do not name grass or reeds, and no console has run this build.

diff --git a/src/video_core/shader_environment.cpp b/src/video_core/shader_environment.cpp
index f1f71bc8e..aadff308b 100644
--- a/src/video_core/shader_environment.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/shader_environment.cpp
@@ -484,6 +484,25 @@ Tegra::Texture::TICEntry GenericEnvironment::ReadTextureInfo(GPUVAddr tic_addr,
 
 namespace {
 
+// NVN keeps the draw's base vertex, base instance and draw ID in c0 0x640/0x644/0x648 (the HLE
+// draw macros map the same slots). Read them from the draw instead: the c0 copy a shader sees can
+// lag the macro's writes, which dropped Ocarina of Time's instanced vegetation.
+std::optional<Shader::ReplaceConstant> ForcedDrawParameter(u32 bank, u32 offset) {
+    if (bank != 0) {
+        return std::nullopt;
+    }
+    switch (offset) {
+    case 0x640:
+        return Shader::ReplaceConstant::BaseVertex;
+    case 0x644:
+        return Shader::ReplaceConstant::BaseInstance;
+    case 0x648:
+        return Shader::ReplaceConstant::DrawID;
+    default:
+        return std::nullopt;
+    }
+}
+
 // Reads a native program a 4 KiB page at a time instead of one 16-byte instruction at a time.
 // Each page is read with ReadBlock, so GPU-written code is flushed first, once per page instead
 // of once per instruction. An instruction that is not inside a fully mapped page is left to the
@@ -942,6 +961,9 @@ u32 GraphicsEnvironment::ReadCbufValue(u32 cbuf_index, u32 cbuf_offset) {
 
 std::optional<Shader::ReplaceConstant> GraphicsEnvironment::GetReplaceConstBuffer(u32 bank,
                                                                                   u32 offset) {
+    if (const auto forced = ForcedDrawParameter(bank, offset)) {
+        return forced;
+    }
     if (!has_hle_engine_state) {
         return std::nullopt;
     }
@@ -1339,6 +1361,9 @@ std::array<u32, 3> FileEnvironment::WorkgroupSize() const {
 
 std::optional<Shader::ReplaceConstant> FileEnvironment::GetReplaceConstBuffer(u32 bank,
                                                                               u32 offset) {
+    if (const auto forced = ForcedDrawParameter(bank, offset)) {
+        return forced;
+    }
     const u64 key = (static_cast<u64>(bank) << 32) | static_cast<u64>(offset);
     auto it = cbuf_replacements.find(key);
     if (it == cbuf_replacements.end()) {
